        "payload": {
          "description": "About NCR Atleos\nNCR Atleos, headquartered in Atlanta, is a leader in expanding financial access. Our dedicated 20,000 employees optimize the branch, improve operational efficiency and maximize self-service availability for financial institutions and retailers across the globe.\nJob Duties for Software Engineer II\nOverall Description\nTeam member operates with minimal to no supervision in many areas while they still may need some direction in others, especially more complex work.\nGenerally, work is done on a sub-system or well-defined feature within a product road-map.\nTypical Experience Range:\n4 to 7 years\nTypical Education\nBachelor’s Degree in a Technical Discipline\nFunctional Competencies\nRequired Skills:\nHave professional experience of developing applications in client server/ n-tier architecture using .Net Technologies like ASP.Net, C#.Net, C++,ADO.Net and XML Web Services.\nExperience and demonstrated knowledge with RESTful services\nExperience and demonstrated knowledge with SQL and any RDBMs e.g. Oracle, SQL Server.\nKnowledge of distributed source version control system (such as Git, BitBucket, etc.) will be considered as an advantage\nAbility to manage multiple tasks and priorities and delivering on tough deadlines.\nAbility and willingness to travel on international assignments.\nHave professional experience of developing crystal reports.\nExperience in implementing distributed architecture using HADOOP.\nExperience in the implementation of TLS 1.2 protocol\nExperience in designing user interfaces using Angular,React and Ember\nExperience of developing dashboards using Microsoft Power BI tools\nExperience in working on Web servers like IIS 6.0, 7.0\nExpert level skills in debugging techniques\nSkilled in problem solving and troubleshooting with proven ability to enhance and improve existing procedures and practices\nContinuous Improvement\nConsults with own & other teams to collect feedback on work practices\nRecommends new industry-leading practices to improve productivity & efficiency\nReviews code to address issues, using root cause analyses to eliminate them in future\nSeeks out novel & efficient ways of working to develop solutions & products that add value to customers\nQuality Design & Assurance\nAble to communicate operational definition of ‘quality’ to ensure all teams have clear expectations and standards of excellence\nEnsures existing processes are followed, identifies new processes as necessary to meet standards of excellence criteria\nWorks to eliminate critical and high priority defects, ensuring acceptance criteria are met\nUnderstands operational, technical, and functional needs of the product and reviews test cases to deliver a positive end-user experience\nSoftware Design & Development\nConsults with internal & external stakeholders to gather understanding of domain, customer & strategic requirements\nEffectively translates requirements & user stories into SW design, recognizing where gaps in understanding exist that can impact building of code\nDesigns beyond scope if necessary to build right solution\nEvaluates options for re-use of existing SW to accelerate or improve product delivery\nSoftware Engineering Best Practices\nMaintains a deep understanding of the SW development life cycle\nSeeks out knowledge and training to remain current on best practices and technologies\nUtilizes knowledge of engineering best practices to ensure quality throughout the software development life cycle\nProposes modifications to the life cycle based on lessons learned\nUnderstands industry standards and best practices for quality testing and determines the best way to apply them within the organization\nTrouble Shooting\nAnalyzes customers’ problems & develops testable theories to diagnose solution / product code issues\nUtilizes range of strategies, techniques & tools to investigate possible resolutions to solve issues\nDetermines best possible solution for increasingly complex problems, quickly implementing solution to reduce downtime for customer.\nOffers of employment are conditional upon passage of screening criteria applicable to the job.\nEEO Statement\nNCR Atleos is an equal-opportunity employer. It is NCR Atleos policy to hire, train, promote, and pay associates based on their job-related qualifications, ability, and performance, without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, citizenship status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, marital status, age, mental or physical disability, genetic information, medical condition, military or veteran status, or any other factor protected by law.\nStatement to Third Party Agencies\nTo ALL recruitment agencies: NCR Atleos only accepts resumes from agencies on the NCR Atleos preferred supplier list. Please do not forward resumes to our applicant tracking system, NCR Atleos employees, or any NCR Atleos facility. NCR Atleos is not responsible for any fees or charges associated with unsolicited resumes.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467590620": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "THE OPPORTUNITY\nCasechek is on a mission to innovate the implant supply chain and bring greater transparency to the cost of patient care. From procurement to payment, Casechek automates workflows for vendor-supported surgical procedures. Our emergent Bill Only solution provides a comprehensive system of record for hospitals and health systems to manage the complexity of surgical cases involving implantable medical devices, expose hidden expenses, and surface revenue opportunities.\nIn this role, you will design, build, and improve the technology that powers Casechek’s mobile and web products. As a Software Engineer, you will develop scalable cloud-based solutions, contribute to technical architecture and design decisions, and help translate product goals into reliable software. You will collaborate closely with Product, Engineering, and other internal teams to deliver solutions that meet customer and business needs. You will also help strengthen our development practices, code quality, testing standards, and overall technical capabilities.\nYour day-to-day interactions will require strategic thinking, strong communication skills, the ability to leverage data, and comfort managing complex initiatives. You should be adept at navigating new technologies and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver exceptional service and support.\nCasechek is a highly collaborative environment, and our team is also self-motivated and works independently. We strongly believe that great ideas are not created in isolation. Our team interacts with our healthcare customers to understand their needs and ultimately deliver the best user experience possible.\nAbout Us\nCasechek is based out of Chicago’s Fulton Market, but we’re a hybrid, remote, and in-person team.\nWe are highly motivated and passionate about solving healthcare’s messiest problems with new technologies.\nWe value diversity, curiosity, and a passion for learning. The team has a lot of advanced degrees and even a few professional musicians.\nInnovating the implant supply chain is a marathon and not a sprint. We support each other in long-term growth and value developing transferable skills.\nResponsibilities\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, a related field, or equivalent professional experience required.\n5+ years of professional backend software development experience.\nStrong proficiency with TypeScript and Node.js.\nProfessional experience developing applications with NestJS.\nExperience designing, developing, and integrating REST APIs.\nExperience supporting and troubleshooting an AWS-hosted SaaS product.\nExperience building scalable, performant, and reliable software solutions.\nFamiliarity with relational database technologies, data modeling, and database design.\nExperience working in an Agile or Scrum software development environment.\nStrong problem-solving skills and the ability to address complex technical challenges creatively.\nSharp attention to detail and a commitment to writing clean, maintainable, and reliable code.\nExcellent English verbal and written communication skills.\nAbility to collaborate effectively across technical and nontechnical teams.\nAbility to manage multiple priorities and adapt to changing project requirements in a fast-paced environment.\nCommitment to continuous learning and staying current with modern technologies, frameworks, and development practices.\nRequirements\nRequirements\n5-8+ years of experience in B2B SaaS growth marketing, demand generation, or revenue marketing.\nDemonstrated track record of generating qualified pipeline and marketing-influenced revenue in support of an enterprise sales organization.\nStrong analytical and reporting skills, with comfort owning metrics such as qualified pipeline generated, opportunities created, conversion rates, campaign performance, and ROMI.\nHands-on expertise with CRM software and Marketing Automation (Salesforce and Pardot preferred), including lead management and attribution.\nAbility to operate strategically while remaining highly hands-on as an individual contributor.\nExperience in managing 1-3 direct reports is strongly preferred\nExperience in Healthcare strongly preferred: Healthcare Technology, Healthcare Supply Chain, Revenue Cycle, Medical Devices, or Hospital Operations.\nComfortable with MS Excel (analyzing spreadsheets and charts) as well as Microsoft PowerPoint.\nBachelor's degree in Marketing, Business Administration or relevant field. (MBA preferred).\nTech Stack\nNestJS\nAngular\nTypeScript\nNode.js\nPostgreSQL\nAWS\nAWS Lambda\n#Casechek\nBenefits\nWhy You'll Love Working Here\nCompetitive Salary and Annual Bonus\nThe salary range for this role is $100,000 to $125,000 , based on experience, skills, and location.\nOpportunity for Long-Term Incentives (LTI)\nBe part of our success with equity or long-term incentive plans that grow with the company.\n401(k) Match\nInvest in your future with our generous matching program to help you build long-term financial security.\nWork-from-Home Flexibility\nEnjoy the freedom to work where you are most productive with a supportive hybrid option in Chicago or a remote setup nationally.\nFlexible Time Off (Unlimited PTO)\nRecharge and focus on what matters most with unlimited paid time off tailored to your needs.\nParental Leave\nTake time to bond with and care for your growing family with fully paid parental leave options.\nComprehensive Medical and Dental Benefits\nPrioritize your health and well-being with premium plans for you and your family.\nBrand-New Pro-Level Laptop\nReceive top-tier tools and technology to set you up for success from day one.\nAnnual Education Budget\nExpand your skills and knowledge with dedicated funding for courses, certifications, and learning resources.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483422876": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer\nWhat if AI could do more than just write a caption?\nCould it help launch and optimise ads?\nBuild landing pages?\nTurn an idea into copy, static creatives and scripts?\nGenerate UGC-style content?\nAutomate reporting?\nAnswer internal questions?\nHandle repetitive client communication?\nHelp our team make better decisions faster?\nThat’s what we want to find out and build.\nCerealBox is looking for its first in-house AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer : someone who can take a real business problem, figure out the smartest technical solution, build it, launch it, maintain it and continuously improve it as better AI models and tools become available.\nThis isn’t a role where someone gives you a list of tickets every morning.\nYou’ll be expected to ask:\n“Why are we doing this manually?”\n“Can AI solve this?”\n“Should we build it ourselves or integrate an existing tool?”\n“How do we make this 10x better?”\nAnd then actually make it happen. 🚀\nA little about CerealBox\nWe’re a UK-based creative and performance agency working exclusively with charities.\nWe manage digital fundraising and paid media for around 30 charity clients and have already built our own analytics platform, True ROAS , to connect advertising spend with actual donation revenue.\nNow we want to take the next step.\nWe want AI and automation embedded across the business not because it sounds cool, but because it can genuinely help our team work smarter, move faster and deliver better results for charities.\nYour first big responsibility\nYou’ll take ownership of True ROAS , our existing production platform used by our media buyers, creative team and leadership.\nToday, it already handles:\nAttribution between Meta Ads and donation data\nROAS reporting by client, campaign and creative\nThousands of creatives and performance insights\nCommercial and settlement reporting\nScheduled data syncs and API integrations\nCurrency conversion and system monitoring\nYou’ll maintain it, improve it and help decide what it becomes next.\nThen comes the fun part 🤖\nSome of the problems we want you to explore include:\nAI Copywriting: Can AI consistently produce strong advertising copy?\nCreative Generation: Can static ad concepts and designs be automated?\nScript Writing: Can AI develop better hooks, concepts and video scripts?\nUGC: How much of UGC production can be generated using AI?\nVideo Editing: Can AI take raw footage and produce high-quality finished ads?\nMedia Buying: Can an AI agent help launch, monitor and optimise campaigns?\nCreative Ideation: Can AI generate genuinely interesting campaign concepts rather than generic ideas?\nLanding Pages: Can we rapidly generate and optimise fundraising landing pages?\nReporting: Can reporting become almost completely automated?\nInternal AI Assistant: Can we make tools like Toast smarter so our team can simply ask questions and get useful answers?\nClient Communication: Can AI safely respond to common or repetitive queries?\nWorkflow Automation: Can we remove repetitive operational work across the company?\nMeta + LLM Integrations: How can Meta data interact with models such as Claude and other LLMs?\nYou won't necessarily build every idea exactly as described.\nPart of your job is deciding what is actually worth building.\nWhat you’ll do\n🧠 AI & Automation\nIdentify repetitive work that can be automated\nResearch AI tools, APIs, models and agents\nPrototype solutions quickly\nDecide whether we should build, integrate or buy\nTurn successful experiments into reliable production tools\nKeep our AI systems current as models and technologies evolve\n💻 Full-Stack Engineering\nBuild and maintain modern React and TypeScript applications\nOwn backend architecture, APIs and database logic\nWork extensively with PostgreSQL and Supabase\nBuild reliable third-party integrations\nMaintain scheduled jobs and data pipelines\nMonitor failures and make sure systems are reliable and secure\n🎨 Product & UX\nSpeak directly with the people using your tools\nUnderstand the actual problem before writing code\nDesign simple, useful interfaces\nTake features from rough idea → prototype → production\nMeasure whether people actually use what you build\nImprove products based on real feedback\nOur current stack\nFrontend\nReact • Vite • TypeScript • TanStack Router & Query • Tailwind • shadcn/ui\nBackend & Data\nSupabase • PostgreSQL • Edge Functions • pg_cron • Row-Level Security\nHosting\nVercel\nIntegrations\nMeta Marketing API • Fundraising platform APIs • AI/LLM APIs\nWays of working\nGitHub • Pull Requests • AI-assisted development\nAnd yes if you can show us that part of the stack should change, we’re open to the conversation.\nWe’d love to speak to you if you have\n4+ years of professional software engineering experience\nStrong full-stack experience with React and TypeScript\nSolid PostgreSQL, data modelling and API experience\nExperience owning production systems\nExperience integrating third-party APIs\nStrong product thinking — not just coding from specifications\nThe ability to design clean interfaces without waiting for perfect Figma files\nConfidence working independently and making technical decisions\nCuriosity around AI, automation, agents and LLM APIs\nClear communication with non-technical teammates\nEven better if you’ve worked with\nSupabase\nMeta Marketing API\nPerformance marketing or ad-tech\nMarketing analytics\nClaude, OpenAI or other LLM APIs\nAI agents / tool calling / MCP\nData visualisation\nCharity or fundraising technology\nEarly-stage products or agencies\nYou do not need to tick every single box.\nIf you’ve built real products, love figuring things out and can show us interesting things you’ve shipped, we’d still like to hear from you.\nWhat you’ll get\n✨ A genuinely high-ownership role\n🤖 The freedom to experiment with AI and emerging technology\n🚀 The opportunity to build products that are actually used every day\n🌍 Exposure to an international UK-based agency environment\n💡 Direct access to leadership and the people using what you build\n📚 Space to research, test and introduce better technology\n🏖️ 21 days paid annual leave\n❤️ Work that ultimately helps charities raise more money\nWhat success looks like\nWe don’t simply want a longer codebase.\nWe want:\nless repetitive work, better data, smarter tools, faster decisions and AI systems that genuinely make the CerealBox team better at what it does.\nIf reading this already has you thinking, “I know how I’d build that…” we should probably talk. 👀\n📩 Apply with your CV, LinkedIn/GitHub profile and, most importantly, examples of products, automations or AI-powered tools you’ve actually built.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
