          "description": "About Out of Talent\nOut of Talent is a growing recruitment startup focused on connecting businesses with the right talent. We are building our internal technology, tools, and systems to improve operational efficiency and support our company's growth.\nWe are looking for a skilled and motivated Node.js Developer to join our team and help develop, maintain, and improve our internal applications and backend systems.\nJob Description\nAs a Node.js Developer, you will be responsible for developing reliable backend services, designing APIs, integrating third-party services, and building scalable solutions to support our internal business operations.\nYou will work closely with the team to understand business requirements, turn ideas into functional applications, and contribute to the development of efficient and maintainable software solutions.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop, maintain, and optimize backend applications using Node.js.\nDesign, build, and maintain RESTful APIs.\nDevelop server-side logic and integrate frontend applications with backend services.\nDesign and manage databases using MongoDB, PostgreSQL, or MySQL.\nIntegrate third-party APIs and external services as required.\nWrite clean, reusable, well-structured, and maintainable code.\nIdentify, troubleshoot, and resolve bugs and performance issues.\nImplement authentication, authorization, and basic application security practices.\nCollaborate with the team to develop internal tools and automate business workflows.\nTest and maintain application functionality, reliability, and performance.\nUse Git for version control and maintain proper technical documentation.\nContribute ideas to improve existing systems and overall development processes.\nQualifications & Requirements\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field is preferred.\nStrong knowledge of JavaScript and Node.js.\nUnderstanding of asynchronous programming, promises, and event-driven architecture.\nExperience building and integrating RESTful APIs.\nFamiliarity with databases such as MongoDB, PostgreSQL, or MySQL.\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorization, and API security.\nFamiliarity with Git and version control workflows.\nGood problem-solving, debugging, and analytical skills.\nAbility to work independently and collaborate effectively with a team.\nWillingness to learn new technologies and contribute to a growing startup environment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485175099": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe role builds and maintains full-stack systems that ship user-facing products used by thousands of customers daily - spanning backend services, web frontends, and the infrastructure that connects them.\nThe engineer will work across the stack in a product-oriented team, collaborating directly with designers, product managers, and other engineers to take features from design to production without handoffs or gatekeepers.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, build, and ship full-stack features using TypeScript, React, and Node.js, owning delivery from API design to production UI\nDevelop and maintain RESTful and GraphQL APIs backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, with attention to performance, pagination, and schema design\nBuild responsive, accessible front-end interfaces in React with modern tooling (Vite, Next.js, Tailwind CSS), maintaining strong Lighthouse scores and WCAG compliance\nWrite integration and end-to-end tests using Jest, Playwright, or equivalent, and maintain CI pipelines in GitHub Actions\nInstrument services with structured logging, tracing, and metrics (Datadog or similar) to support observability and on-call readiness\nParticipate in code reviews, architecture discussions, and technical design docs; mentor mid-level engineers on the team\nContribute to infrastructure-as-code and deployment workflows in Docker and Kubernetes-based environments\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–6 years of professional software engineering experience shipping production web applications\nStrong proficiency in TypeScript or a similar typed language across both backend and frontend codebases\nHands-on experience with React (or Vue/Svelte) and modern state management patterns\nSolid backend fundamentals: API design, relational databases (PostgreSQL), caching, authentication, and async processing\nExperience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and containerized deployment workflows\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience; track record of owning features end-to-end\nBonus: Experience with mobile development (React Native or Swift/Kotlin), Kubernetes, or prior work in a product-led startup environment",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485699715": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nSynergisticIT is a technology-focused company that supports organizations in meeting their software development, data, and information technology needs. The company works with clients across a range of industries and connects technology professionals with opportunities to contribute to real-world projects. SynergisticIT also helps candidates build practical skills and prepare for careers in the technology sector through professional development and career support.\nAbout The Role\nSynergisticIT is seeking motivated technology professionals for software development and related IT opportunities. Depending on the assignment, successful candidates may contribute to application design, implementation, testing, deployment, or ongoing support. This role is suited to individuals who enjoy solving problems, learning new tools, and working collaboratively to deliver dependable technology solutions.\nTeam members may work with experienced engineers, project stakeholders, and client teams to understand requirements and turn them into maintainable technical outcomes. The specific technologies, responsibilities, and project environment may vary based on client needs. Candidates should be comfortable adapting to evolving priorities and communicating progress, questions, and potential risks clearly. The role offers opportunities to apply existing knowledge while continuing to develop technical and professional capabilities.\nQualifications\nCandidates should have a degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience. Applicants should demonstrate foundational knowledge of programming concepts, data structures, algorithms, databases, and software development practices. Experience or familiarity with one or more programming languages, such as Java, Python, JavaScript, or C#, is valuable. Knowledge of web technologies, cloud platforms, version control, testing, or agile methodologies may also be relevant, depending on the assignment.\nStrong analytical thinking and attention to detail are important. Candidates should be able to explain technical ideas clearly, work productively with others, and respond constructively to feedback. A willingness to learn unfamiliar tools and technologies, manage competing tasks, and take responsibility for assigned work is expected. Professional communication and a collaborative approach are essential.\nResponsibilities\nResponsibilities may include reviewing project requirements and contributing to technical approaches; writing, testing, debugging, and maintaining software code; and helping develop or enhance applications, services, and internal tools. Team members may work with databases and APIs, prepare technical documentation, and use version-control and issue-tracking tools to coordinate their work.\nAdditional duties may include participating in code reviews, development meetings, and project planning; investigating software defects and supporting their resolution; and collaborating with engineers, quality assurance professionals, product stakeholders, and client representatives. Employees are expected to follow established development and security practices, communicate delivery risks promptly, and contribute to continuous improvement. Specific duties will depend on the position and project to which a candidate is assigned.\nBenefits\nSynergisticIT offers the opportunity to develop technology skills while pursuing professional opportunities in a changing industry. Depending on the role, assignment, and employment arrangement, candidates may have access to career guidance, technical learning resources, mentorship, and opportunities to work with client teams. Compensation, benefits, work location, and other employment terms vary by position and will be shared during the hiring process. Candidates are encouraged to discuss role-specific details with the recruiting team.\nEqual Opportunity\nSynergisticIT is committed to fair and inclusive employment practices. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, skills, experience, and business needs. Applicants will be considered without discrimination on the basis of legally protected characteristics under applicable laws. The company welcomes candidates from diverse backgrounds and encourages all qualified individuals to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T17:08:03.344902+00:00"
  },
